<h1>homeomorphic</h1>
<p>
(definition)
</p>

<p>
<strong>Definition:</strong>
Two <a href="graph.html"><em>graphs</em></a> are homeomorphic if they can be made <a href="isomorphic.html"><em>isomorphic</em></a> by inserting new <a href="vertex.html"><em>vertices</em></a> of <a href="degree.html"><em>degree</em></a> 2 into <a href="edge.html"><em>edges</em></a>.
</p>


<p>
<em>Note:
This corresponds to the topological notion since adding or removing degree 2 vertices doesn't change the graph's topology. </p> 
<p> This is similar to, but not the same as, homomorphic.</em>
</p>

<p>Author: <a href="../Other/contrib.html#authorPEB">PEB</a></p>
